  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FAO HUM 2017-2020 - FAO HUM 2020</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">FAO HUM 2017-2020</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Detta beslut avser en st&#xf6;rre &#xe4;ndring av insats  mellan Sida och FAO f&#xf6;r att m&#xf6;jligg&#xf6;ra humanit&#xe4;rt st&#xf6;d i tre kriser under 2020 (Afghanistan, Nigeria och Somalia). St&#xf6;det omfattar ocks&#xe5; oallokerad finansiering till FAO:s s&#xe4;rskilda fond f&#xf6;r katastrofer och rehabilitering, SFERA, som &#xe4;r ytterligare en mekanism f&#xf6;r att tillg&#xe4;ngligg&#xf6;ra st&#xf6;d till FAO i h&#xe4;ndelser av akuta kriser. Sida kommer under 2020 att fortsatt engagera sig i att st&#xe4;rka det humanit&#xe4;ra systemet genom att finansiering till det globala mats&#xe4;kerhetsklustret (gFSC). FAO:s kontor f&#xf6;r utv&#xe4;rdering (OED) kommer under 2020 att genomf&#xf6;ra en utv&#xe4;rdering av de fem Sida-finansierade projekten i Sahel (Tchad, Kamerun, Mali och Niger).
 
Beslutet omfattar finansiellt st&#xf6;d till FAO om 67 683 193 SEK.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a &#x201c;Major Amendment of Contribution&#x201d; between Sida and FAO to allow for humanitarian response in three crises (Afghanistan, Nigeria and Somalia) for 2020.
This Amendment also includes support for unallocated funding to FAO&apos;s Special Fund for
Emergency and Rehabilitation (SFERA), capacity-building support to the global Food Security Cluster (gFSC) and funding for evaluation in regard to FAO Sida multi-year resilience projects in the Sahel. This Decision concerns a financial contribution to FAO amounting to 67,683,193 Swedish
kronor (SEK).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The three main drivers of food crises in 2020 were conflict and insecurity,
economic shocks due to the compounding effects of the coronavirus
disease 2019 (COVID-19), and weather extremes. Households that depend on
farming and pastoralism for their livelihoods continue to be among the worst
affected, with their livelihoods, food security and nutrition at serious risk. To
protect and restore peoples agricultural livelihoods and increase their resilience to
threats and crises, the Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations
(FAO) works to improve preparedness, implement effective response and promote
sustainable recovery. In order to achieve this, FAO is among the organizations
leading global efforts in anticipatory action, an approach that translates early
warnings into activities that reduce the impact of disasters. By investing in
agricultural production  critical to enhancing food security, nutrition and income
generation  FAOs support before and during emergencies saves livelihoods and
builds resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
